WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.320
Hi there, Steve Kaufmann here, and
today I'm going to talk about the

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:07.530
most important thing in language
learning, and that is enjoyment.

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:12.180
Enjoyment is not only the goal of
language learning, enjoyment is how you

00:00:12.185 --> 00:00:14.220
manage to succeed in language learning.

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:19.620
And I'm gonna talk about the five stages
of enjoyment because after all, as

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:23.370
we go through learning the language,
we are in different stages of either

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:26.610
we're beginning the language or we're
starting to get ahold of the language.

00:00:26.615 --> 00:00:28.820
And there are different
kinds of enjoyment.

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:31.845
At least that's how I
experience language learning.

00:00:31.905 --> 00:00:38.925
So when we begin the first stage, when
we're starting to discover the language,

00:00:38.985 --> 00:00:45.945
at first it's all noise, but somehow as
if by magic, what was noise becomes words,

00:00:46.425 --> 00:00:51.224
uh, you start to be able to read a little
bit even though you listen many, many

00:00:51.224 --> 00:00:55.875
times and keep on missing the same parts
of what you're listening to and, and you

00:00:55.879 --> 00:01:00.389
look up words, let's say on LingQ, and
you review them and you listen again.

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:01.559
And...

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:04.170
but it's exciting.

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:09.360
It's, it's that excitement of discovering
something new and, and that's in the

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:14.220
first stage of learning a language
that kind of maintains me because

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:17.670
so much of it is, is not meaning.

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:23.100
It's, it's unclear and, and it, it
just seems so strange at first, and

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:26.350
particularly when I was learning Persian
and Arabic with different writing

00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:28.815
systems, it's so difficult at first.

00:01:28.815 --> 00:01:32.445
However, there's that enjoyment,
that excitement of, of sort of,

00:01:32.445 --> 00:01:33.914
I'm embarking on something new.

00:01:33.914 --> 00:01:34.845
I'm gonna learn this.

00:01:35.145 --> 00:01:40.365
What to me is an exotic language and, and
I find that initial period very enjoyable.

00:01:40.545 --> 00:01:45.945
And so there is that first period of
enjoyment of discovering something new.

00:01:46.585 --> 00:01:50.354
But then after a while, we get
tired of listening to the same

00:01:50.354 --> 00:01:51.645
stuff over and over again.

00:01:51.765 --> 00:01:55.665
There's a lot of repetitive listening
in the early stages in order to, you

00:01:55.665 --> 00:01:57.565
know, to get a hold of the new language.

00:01:57.795 --> 00:02:03.315
So in that second stage, all of a sudden
what we have been listening to, even

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:07.485
though we don't really understand it
all that well, it's becoming familiar.

00:02:07.785 --> 00:02:11.685
We're going to, we're going back to
something that's no longer brand new.

00:02:11.685 --> 00:02:13.005
In fact, it's familiar.

00:02:13.275 --> 00:02:15.705
Still we understand 10, 15%.

00:02:16.755 --> 00:02:20.505
It seems like there's an endless number
of words to learn, but it's a familiar.

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:27.015
And, and I enjoy that challenge when
I'm starting to get a bit of a sense

00:02:27.015 --> 00:02:31.185
of the language and it's familiar,
familiar sounds, listening to the

00:02:31.185 --> 00:02:35.084
same sounds that I don't understand,
struggling with the same writing

00:02:35.084 --> 00:02:40.275
system that still presents challenges,
uh, but it's a familiar environment.

00:02:40.275 --> 00:02:42.255
I, I miss it when I'm away from it.

00:02:42.315 --> 00:02:48.355
I enjoy going back to it, even as the
language remains very unclear for me, I

00:02:48.355 --> 00:02:53.575
enjoy that second period as we're starting
to turn the corner in the language.

00:02:54.735 --> 00:03:00.225
Now, the third period, which is kind
of that long plateau, which for some

00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:02.985
people can be a period of frustration.

00:03:03.255 --> 00:03:07.005
For me, it's, it's not a period of
frustration because I'm now in a

00:03:07.010 --> 00:03:12.374
situation where I understand, depending
on the content, you know, 20, 30,

00:03:12.375 --> 00:03:17.835
40, 50% of some content, if I go back
to some of my earlier, sort of, mini

00:03:17.835 --> 00:03:23.445
stories in LingQ where I've heard them
so many times, I understand 70%, 80%.

00:03:23.565 --> 00:03:27.105
And every time I listen, I pick up
something new of my old beginner

00:03:27.110 --> 00:03:31.755
material, and then I push myself forward
into new and more difficult material.

00:03:32.115 --> 00:03:36.825
And, and I'm starting to feel that
I am going to be able to understand

00:03:36.825 --> 00:03:41.965
that language, even though the
language still is a bit opaque.

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:48.045
It's still not really comprehensible,
but I recognize that I understand a

00:03:48.045 --> 00:03:50.234
lot more than I understood before.

00:03:50.445 --> 00:03:54.105
I almost feel as if I shouldn't
understand it, but I don't fully, I

00:03:54.109 --> 00:03:57.345
understand some words, but I can't
get a sense of the whole meaning.

00:03:57.554 --> 00:04:02.475
But still it's enjoyable because
I sense that I'm on the verge of

00:04:02.475 --> 00:04:07.214
reaching, you know, a level of,
of comfortable comprehension.

00:04:07.304 --> 00:04:10.085
I'm not there yet, but I
think I'm gonna get there.

00:04:10.615 --> 00:04:14.910
So that sort of plateau period, which
is quite long, it seems there's an

00:04:14.915 --> 00:04:16.680
endless number of words to learn.

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:21.719
It doesn't bother me 'cause I know
that if I continue with my good

00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:25.919
language learning habits, if I continue
listening and reading, just as I've

00:04:25.919 --> 00:04:30.240
already progressed from where I was
before, I will continue to progress.

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:32.840
The brain is getting used to the language.

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:35.490
The brain is already much more
used to the language than it

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:37.140
was in the previous stages.

00:04:37.890 --> 00:04:42.255
Now the fourth stage, which is in
many cases, you know, as far as

00:04:42.255 --> 00:04:45.895
people go, it's as far as I have
gone in a number of my languages.

00:04:46.125 --> 00:04:54.344
It's where I understand 80% of most,
uh, language content, uh, of movies.

00:04:54.705 --> 00:04:58.815
It can vary, but let's say
60, 70, 80%, I understand.

00:04:58.995 --> 00:05:01.895
I'm comfortable if I'm in a
conversation with someone.

00:05:02.035 --> 00:05:07.125
I can hold up my end of the conversation,
I understand what the person is saying.

00:05:07.335 --> 00:05:09.525
I'm able to get my meaning across.

00:05:09.765 --> 00:05:14.895
Sometimes, you know, with mistakes or
sometimes I can't remember words, and

00:05:14.895 --> 00:05:18.284
sometimes I don't understand some of the
things that are said to me, but by and

00:05:18.289 --> 00:05:20.775
large, I am functional in the language.

00:05:20.955 --> 00:05:24.925
I meant B2, call it almost B2.

00:05:24.945 --> 00:05:28.604
I'm functional, and if I leave
the language there, I've got

00:05:28.604 --> 00:05:30.864
something that I can come back to.

00:05:31.224 --> 00:05:34.995
So that's a sense of, you know,
achievement accomplishment.

00:05:35.295 --> 00:05:38.985
It's, it's for, in many languages,
it's the end of the line.

00:05:38.985 --> 00:05:39.825
I made it.

00:05:40.185 --> 00:05:46.335
If I leave it and let it slide into
disuse, if again, I'm in a situation

00:05:46.335 --> 00:05:48.555
where I need it, I can bring it back.

00:05:48.555 --> 00:05:50.055
So I can tick it off.

00:05:50.055 --> 00:05:51.795
This is a language that I have learned.

00:05:51.915 --> 00:05:54.135
That doesn't mean I'm
perfect, but I've learned it.

00:05:54.195 --> 00:05:56.295
So that's stage four of enjoyment.

00:05:56.595 --> 00:06:02.070
Now, stage five, which is the
ultimate, is when you are totally

00:06:02.070 --> 00:06:03.210
comfortable in the language.

00:06:03.419 --> 00:06:05.580
You understand the movies.

00:06:05.849 --> 00:06:08.039
You can be in any situation at any time.

00:06:08.039 --> 00:06:10.919
You cannot speak the language for
two years and you come back to

00:06:10.919 --> 00:06:13.950
it and you're just about where
you were when you left off.

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:16.740
Uh, this is like, I call it a C1.

00:06:17.010 --> 00:06:20.219
This is where I feel, you know,
and I can listen to literature,

00:06:20.219 --> 00:06:23.310
I can read literature, I can do
whatever I want in the language.

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:25.950
That is sort of the ultimate.

00:06:25.979 --> 00:06:30.705
Now you don't have to achieve
that in the language in order to

00:06:30.705 --> 00:06:34.845
enjoy the process of learning the
language or to enjoy the language.

00:06:35.025 --> 00:06:37.125
I enjoy the language at the beginning.

00:06:37.335 --> 00:06:41.745
If I start another language, uh,
might be Hindi or something, I'm

00:06:41.745 --> 00:06:46.095
gonna enjoy that initial period of
discovery, then I'm gonna enjoy that

00:06:46.100 --> 00:06:49.275
second stage when it's familiar.

00:06:49.335 --> 00:06:52.755
It's a familiar struggle, but
it's a familiar environment.

00:06:52.755 --> 00:06:53.385
I don't mind that.

00:06:53.385 --> 00:06:54.105
I enjoy that.

00:06:54.405 --> 00:06:59.130
Then when I'm on that long plateau,
where it seems as if I'm not progressing

00:06:59.250 --> 00:07:02.970
and yet I'm understanding more and
more I feel as if I should understand.

00:07:02.970 --> 00:07:05.010
I almost understand,
but I don't understand.

00:07:06.090 --> 00:07:10.530
Uh, but then the fourth stage is
when I'm kind of at, almost at

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:13.440
the final stage of my journey.

00:07:13.770 --> 00:07:16.080
I'm comfortable, I'm
happy I can tick it off.

00:07:16.110 --> 00:07:16.830
It's mine.

00:07:17.415 --> 00:07:21.915
But then with some languages, if I
get the opportunity, I'll push myself

00:07:22.035 --> 00:07:23.705
through to that final stage of enjoy...

00:07:24.015 --> 00:07:24.495
enjoyment.

00:07:24.585 --> 00:07:26.565
But all stages are enjoyable.

00:07:26.685 --> 00:07:32.355
And enjoying the language learning
process is not only the key to success,

00:07:32.505 --> 00:07:34.665
but it also should be the goal.

00:07:34.815 --> 00:07:39.225
So thank you for listening, and if
you enjoy my, uh, enjoy my videos,

00:07:39.225 --> 00:07:41.015
please um, you know, subscribe.

00:07:42.015 --> 00:07:45.315
And I'll leave you with, uh, a
couple of videos that I've done

00:07:45.315 --> 00:07:47.425
on a similar subject in the past.

00:07:47.765 --> 00:07:48.485
Bye for now.

